--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why the GPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Switcher's video engine links libobs (the core of OBS Studio), which is licensed
under the GNU General Public License version 2. A release also ships libobs and
a set of OBS plugins in `obs-runtime/`. The combined work is therefore governed
by the GPL.

In practical terms, anyone who receives a binary is entitled to the complete
corresponding source — both this project's source and the source of the exact
libobs build that is bundled with it.

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the full component inventory, including one open
question about the proprietary NDI library that must be resolved before a public
release.

